; tests/gen-query-flow-find-band.fk — the FIND lane of the generated queries.
;
; PROOF LEVEL: GO AND RUST ONLY. A find query returns a NODE ID, ~3.0e9, past
; 2^31. The TypeScript kernel's recipe walker is I32 by design
; (form-kernel-ts/src/compiler.ts:268 `int: n | 0`; line 423 "I32 default … to
; keep V8's SMI tagging"), so it returns 3045007003 as -1249960293. Minimal
; repro: (walk_recipe (intern_trivial_int 3045007003)).
;
; This is a BODY-WIDE constraint, not a fault of this cell: every lnsi-node
; graph lands above 2^31 (giles-light-hubs at 3041xxxxxx), so any of them walked
; as a recipe truncates on that arm.
;
; preludes: form-stdlib/core.fk cognition/language-neutral-symbol-identity.fk cognition/steiner-neutral-kernel.fk cognition/gen-neutral-code.fk cognition/gen-query-flow.fk
;
; Verdict 3 on Go / Rust:
;   all four find questions agree with the hand-written accessor, on the
;     real graph, including the one with NO answer                       1
;   and a returned node id really is above 2^31 — the value this lane
;     exists to carry, stated so the constraint cannot be forgotten      2
(do
    (gqy-check-find))
